      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Yellow Submarine (1968) revolutionized animation with its psychedelic Pop Art style that perfectly captured The Beatles' most experimental period. The film blends Peter Max-inspired visuals with groundbreaking techniques from animation director George Dunning, creating a kaleidoscopic journey that influenced everything from Pink Floyd - The Wall (1982) to <a href=\"/movie/324857\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"324857\">Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse</a> (2018). The Blue Meanies' invasion of Pepperland serves as a clever allegory for conformity versus artistic freedom, while sequences like \"Lucy in the Sky with Diamonds\" and \"Eleanor Rigby\" set new standards for translating music into surreal visual storytelling."
      },
      {
